Z||000013||Raydar||09-13-2000||11:16 PM||||Monkeyman, I know what you mean. An Impala is only marginally smaller than some SUVs. And waaayyyyyy uglier, IMHO. The tail lights, anyway.<BR>When I had my first Fiero (also an 85 GT), I never really paid any attention to how low it was, until I found myself behind an MGB, and was <I>looking up</I> at it.<BR>Excursions scare the hell out of me, although they are soooo expensive (and huge)that they are not real common here, yet.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Standard||09-15-2000||05:46 AM||||I just drove a friends Supra the other day, and I felt like I was driving a truck!  It just <I>feels</I> so much bigger than my Fiero.  come to think of it, it is a bit bigger  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.. not to mention the twitchy power steering and the shifter that had absolutly no feel to it.. I can't stand Import gearbox's.. gear spacing is waaay to wide, no feel what-so-ever... anywho.. back on topic.. I like being lower than everybody  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>oh wait.. this thread was about oil... uhhhh.... I think my GT is running a bit low.. I should check it sometime..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
